        "calls": 3,
        "title": "Rename COD-760 first party and house verdict fields in ads fetch",
        "summary": "The `ADS_FETCH_COMPLETED_FIELDS` allowlist in `common/src/util/axiom-only-log.ts` renames `first_party_outcome` to `direct_result` and `house_outcome` to `house_result`, aligning the field names with the existing `direct_` prefix convention on `no_fill_reason` codes. The accompanying `no_fill_reason` doc comment replaces the previous `first_party_`/`house_`-prefixed verdict codes with a fresh enumerated set (`direct_` + `direct_result`, `house_campaign_empty`, `timed_out`, `no_paid_source_asked`, etc.). The decision-contract test keeps the COD-760 stage verdicts on fetch completion verifies the renamed fields are emitted and the old names are no longer allowlisted.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In `common/src/util/axiom-only-log.ts`, the `ADS_FETCH_COMPLETED_FIELDS` allowlist renames `first_party_outcome` to `direct_result` and `house_outcome` to `house_result`, and the `no_fill_reason` doc comment replaces the old `first_party_`/`house_`-prefixed verdict codes with a new enumerated code set (`direct_`, `house_campaign_empty`, `timed_out`, `no_paid_source_asked`, etc.). The test keeps the COD-760 stage verdicts on fetch completion in `common/src/util/__tests__/axiom-only-log.test.ts` asserts the renamed fields are present and the old names are gone.",
